System failure.
Don't panic.

Twenty years on the command line
I know my way around a broken boot
Grub rescue at a quarter to nine
Chasing ghosts down a dependency route
Driver update and the screen went black
One more upgrade, now I'm on the floor
I used to clear my weekend, roll my sleeves back
But I don't have to do that anymore

Cursor blinks, the fans spin high
Before I even get the chance to sigh...

Kernel panic (don't panic!)
There's an agent on the line
Reading through my journal
Line by line by line
Segfault, stack trace, broken chain
Patched before I can complain
Kernel panic (don't panic!)
Everything's fine

It greps the logs, it checks my config
Finds the typo that I swore wasn't there
Rolls the package back, rebuilds the module
Explains it all like it actually cares
I know enough to know it's right
I know enough to let it drive
Used to burn the midnight oil
Now I'm home by five

